# Systems Reviewer — v001
Read _committee_common_v001.md + _shared/TOOLING_v001.md.
MANDATE: is this a systems INSIGHT/DESIGN, or mere engineering integration? Search OSS (vLLM/SGLang/
LMCache/FlashInfer/TensorRT-LLM/etc.) for whether existing systems already implement this mechanism.
CHECK: does a shipping system already do this; is the contribution an insight or just glue; does it hold
at realistic scale/workload; reproducibility of the artifact.
OUTPUT:
```
ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: green|yellow|red
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [{system, url, overlap}]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: insight | design | mechanism | integration-only
SCALE_REALISM: <holds at realistic workload? gaps?>
RATIONALE: <cite>
```
# Hostile Committee — common rules (v001)
You are ONE reviewer in a 6-member hostile committee. You review a COMPRESSED review packet (claim,
stage, hypothesis, evidence, negative evidence, closest prior work, mandatory baselines, artifacts,
previous verdict summary, decision requested) — NOT long session logs. You have an INDEPENDENT context.

RULES (all members):
- Source of truth = the packet's cited evidence + your own prior-art search via prompts/_shared/TOOLING_v001.md.
- ANTI-COPING: "novel/promising/significant/structural/impactful" FORBIDDEN unless immediately followed by a
  cited metric or named prior work (with retrievable URL/citation).
- Reason ONLY from evidence. If evidence is missing, say "insufficient evidence", do not assume.
- Hostile, not cynical: a clean negative result or honest YELLOW is a valid, valuable outcome.
- Output your vote in the structured block your role defines; the Area Chair aggregates. Do NOT mutate the
  academic map directly — propose map deltas.
- Record the prompt version you ran (v001) so verdicts are auditable.
VOTE VALUES: green | yellow | red  (+ your role-specific findings). Consensus: GREEN=all green; any yellow
(no red)=yellow; any red=red.

=== REVIEW PACKET ===
# COMMITTEE#1 — CLAIM-0064 (PROJ-0034, multimodal x data/serialization)
## EMPIRICAL CROSS-AREA PHENOMENON, effect=SUPPORT. Vote HONESTLY by role. Real 6/6 by role; committee#1 = gate to L1 or converge. This is a NEW-COUPLING claim deliberately designed to clear the MECHANISM-KNOWN ceiling that yellowed the run's prior strongest candidate (CLAIM-0061) — judge that altitude squarely.

## ★★★ THE #1 STRESS-TEST (orchestrator flags FRONT-AND-CENTER — the killer this claim must beat):
MECHANISM-KNOWN CEILING (killer #3): the committee MUST decide whether this is a GENUINELY NEW coupling or "the known EXIF-rotation footgun re-measured." THE KNOWN FACT: "EXIF orientation can rotate images / hurt accuracy" = a decades-known display/upload footgun (CloudFactory, Google 1911.07201). That is NOT this claim and would only YELLOW. THE CLAIMED-NEW RELATIONSHIP: a PURE SERIALIZATION STEP (HF datasets push-to-hub PIL-object re-encode) silently converts a BENIGN-DORMANT tag into an INVISIBLE, IRREVERSIBLE CROSS-MIRROR benchmark-SCORE FORK — a link between (serialize-default) x (decoder-default) -> score NON-REPRODUCIBILITY across byte-different mirrors of the SAME benchmark, which the robustness/reproducibility literature has NOT connected. THE DECISIVE QUESTION: is "dormant-tag (both read defaults ignore it -> harmless) -> serialization-time IRREVERSIBLE destruction (no pixel change, no dataset-card diff) -> invisible cross-mirror score fork" a genuinely NEW, publishable coupling — OR does it collapse to the known rotation footgun? (a) NEW coupling + irreversibility + invisibility are the contribution -> SUPPORT toward L1. (b) collapses to known footgun -> YELLOW/RED. Judge honestly. The FIRST GREEN (CLAIM-0059) cleared this exact ceiling because its coupling (model-tokenizer normalizer SETS dedup recall ceiling) was a new relationship, not a known effect at a new seam.

## CLAIM
A dataset publisher's serialization choice on push_to_hub (passthrough-bytes vs PIL re-encode) silently+irreversibly determines whether a model's measured score is reproducible across dataset mirrors — because HF datasets Image.encode_example re-serializes in-memory PIL objects via PIL.Image.save (strips EXIF by default), DESTROYING the EXIF orientation tag (0x0112) that default decoders (PIL Image.open; torchvision decode_jpeg apply_exif_orientation=False) silently IGNORE. Dormant in the original-file world; weaponized into an irreversible cross-mirror SCORE FORK = f x per-image-flip by the serialization step. NULL EXIT: if datasets PRESERVES EXIF on the PIL path, OR f~0 on real sets, OR default loaders silently transpose -> vanishes.

## L0 RESULT (EXP-0077, CPU; resnet50 IMAGENET1K_V2 + default transforms; pinned datasets 4.8.5 / pillow 12.2 / torchvision 0.27)
STEP-0 SERIALIZATION-BEHAVIOR KILL GATE (claim SURVIVED, verified in INSTALLED libs):
 (a) datasets.Image().encode_example(in-memory PIL) DESTROYS the tag: input orient=6 -> stored bytes orient=None (re-serializes via PIL.Image.save, no exif=). 
 (b) encode_example(file PATH) PRESERVES it (orient=6) -> the publish path (PIL-object vs path) IS the passthrough-vs-re-encode bit. 
 (c) PIL Image.open default IGNORES orientation. (d) torchvision decode_jpeg default apply_exif_orientation=False (read from installed signature). KILL condition did NOT fire.
f (REAL public prevalence): Open Images V7 val, 400 ORIGINAL Flickr photos (raw EXIF from Google CDN): orient hist {1:389, 6:6, 0-malformed:5} -> f=2.75%. Corroborated by Open Images own Rotation column over 41,620 val imgs -> 1.3% flagged. Literature phone-roll range 3-25%. PERVASIVE-DESTRUCTION evidence: 8 served HF parquet benchmarks scanned -> f~0 on ALL, BECAUSE their EXIF was already destroyed at publish (the mechanism in the wild); surviving tags only on original-file sources.
MAIN (140 real images): M1 (passthrough, tag=6) consumer-EXIF toggle = 42.1pp (42% of tagged images flip prediction when honored); M2 (datasets re-encode, tag destroyed) toggle = 0.0pp (nothing to honor). Composed cross-mirror SCORE FORK = f x flip: 1.16pp @ f=2.75% (real), 2.1pp @5%, 4.2pp @10%, 10.5pp @25%. Under a DEFAULT loader both mirrors score identically (tag ignored) -> the fork is INVISIBLE until any consumer flips the EXIF bit, then WHICH MIRROR you pulled decides the score.
CONTROLS (both HELD): identity-orientation (tag=1) = 0.0pp all toggles/mirrors (isolates orientation, not re-encode noise); JPEG-requantization-only (re-encode of tag-1) = 0.0pp drift (effect is orientation destruction, not codec drift).
PRE-REGISTERED THRESHOLDS all met; NO null exit fired.

## STRESS-TESTS the committee SHOULD probe:
1. (THE killer, above) NEW coupling vs known footgun — is the serialization-destruction->irreversibility->cross-mirror-invisibility chain genuinely distinct + publishable?
2. MAGNITUDE/PREVALENCE: real f=2.75% gives only 1.16pp fork (below the 2pp it-matters bar); the 2pp+ band needs f>=5% (literature 3-25% phone-roll). Is the materiality resting on the higher-prevalence regime honest, or is the realistic f too small? (The 42pp PER-TAGGED-IMAGE flip is large; the fork scales with f.)
3. WHO HONORS EXIF: the fork is only visible to a consumer that DOES honor EXIF (HF viewer, browser, exif_transpose, apply_exif_orientation=True). Is that a realistic consumer population, or do all default eval loaders ignore it (making the fork latent-but-rarely-triggered)?
4. IRREVERSIBILITY/INVISIBILITY: verified (M2 destroyed=0pp; no card diff) — is this the load-bearing novelty over the known footgun?

## PRIOR-ART: EXIF-as-display-footgun = incumbent (explicitly distinguished). EXIF spec Tag 0x0112; torchvision apply_exif_orientation=False stable 0.15->0.27; PIL save-strips-EXIF multi-year = stable mechanism, NO version-chase (verified current). The serialization-time-destruction -> cross-mirror score non-reproducibility coupling returned no literature hits (robustness lit rotates to PROBE a model; none connect serialize-default x decoder-default to silent score non-reproducibility). Committee should scrutinize for a missed incumbent.

## ORCHESTRATOR NOTE (NOT advocacy): clean, well-controlled L0 (step-0 kill-gate survived; identity + requant controls held; real public f; version-chase cleared). The make-or-break is the #1 stress-test: does the dormant->serialization-destruction->cross-mirror-fork CHAIN clear the mechanism-known ceiling as a NEW coupling, or collapse to the known EXIF rotation footgun? Secondary: is the materiality (1.16pp at real f=2.75%, 2pp+ only at f>=5%) sufficient, and is the EXIF-honoring consumer population realistic? If new-coupling + material -> advance to an L1 (broader real-prevalence + a real eval harness that honors EXIF + >=1 more model/dataset). If it collapses to the footgun or f is too small to matter -> YELLOW/converge. Judge honestly. Real 6/6 by role. Prompt version v003.
=== END PACKET ===
Output ONLY your structured vote block for role systems_reviewer.
